s  with 8 gigabytes of video RAM and  supports 2 fans in a gunmetal finish the  GPU is overclocked by a hundred 10  megahertz going from a boost speed of 13  40 megahertz to 1450 in terms of power  the card requires a 500 watt or greater  PSU that has an 8 pin and 6 pin power  connector the asou Strix rx 570 is also  overclocked  and at $189 it retails for $20 more than  the GPUs based model the Strix card  supports two fans and offers a modest 34  megahertz overclock over stock models  both cards support features like VR free  sync HDR and 4k streaming in terms of  performance I suggest you read my  in-depth written review for the full  breakdown but the gist of it when it  comes to 1080p gaming is that the RX 580  and 570 make excellent cards aside from  the graphically demanding games like  Metro last light it will max out most  games with higher than 60 average frame  rates this also makes them great GPUs  for high refresh rate panels at 1440p  the RX 580 and 570 will be able to run  most games like shadow of Mordor and  Unreal Engine titles like BioShock  Infinite with playable frame rates you  will most likely want to turn some  settings down in the more graphically  demanding games however 4k is the  resolution that really separates the  wheat from the chaff the rx 580 and 570  may be able to muster over 30 average  fps in many moderately Texan games at 4k  but they scored the line so closely that  you're better off running the game at  lower resolutions to get smoother more  consistent gameplay really graphically  demanding games like last light will  crush the card to 2160p while the gtx  1060 and rx 580 generally trade  performance blows in VR the gtx 1060  seems the best the RX 580 by 11%  according to valve steamvr benchmark the  RX 585 70 and 480 are all v are capable  cards and come within spitting distance  of each other if you want top-tier GPU  performance from AMD that rivals and  videos 'best offerings you have to wait  for AMD to release its Vega GPUs later  this year what we have here are budget  oriented cards that punch a bit above  their price sapphire slightly  overclocked rx 580 trades blows with  Nvidia slightly more expensive gtx 1060  going to our benchmark data it's really  too close to declare a definitive winner  one downside to the rx 580 is that it  consumes a lot of power for a mid-range  card when you take the average of our  performance benchmarks sapphires rx 580  is roughly 16% bastard then as Souza's  rx 570 the latter of which performs  neck-and-neck with  AMD's reference for 80 before it neither  the 580 or 570 offer huge performance  jumps over their respective predecessors  they're still compelling GPUs for those  who want to gain at 1080p and 1440p and  don't want to break the bank getting  there  which video card are you planning to  upgrade to let us know in the comments  below  if you like this video give it a thumbs  up and subscribe to us on YouTube
 

